cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this simulator or build on these results, please cite it as below."
title: "FoveaRL: A Simulation Study of Reward Design for Reinforcement-Learning-Based Foveated Streaming in VR Teleoperation of Mobile Robots"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Rishi Jayanath A"
  - name: "Adwaith Sajikumar"
  - name: "Anirudh M R"
  - name: "Ashish Mathew"
  - name: "Jeremy Joe Thomas"
  - name: "R Priscilla Joy"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rishijayanath24-cpu/FoveaRL"
url: "https://rishijayanath24-cpu.github.io/FoveaRL/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - virtual reality
  - teleoperation
  - foveated streaming
  - reinforcement learning
  - mobile robots
  - reward design
abstract: >-
  Simulation study of reward design for double-DQN agents that adapt foveation
  radius, peripheral resolution and bitrate for VR teleoperation of a mobile
  robot over variable networks. A latency-aware quality-of-experience reward
  matched the strongest fixed setting on task success; a task-aware reward with
  a control-error term was markedly worse, and ablations isolate that term as
  the cause.
